::JOUR_U05_L01_Q_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.01] Source: Presentation Plan: Transit Safety Report. Reporting Topic: Students crossing the east parking lot after dismissal. Source Notes: The school safety aide counted thirty-seven students crossing between parked cars on Tuesday. Two students said the marked crosswalk is hard to see when buses are lined up. The assistant principal said the school can add temporary cones while it reviews permanent signs. Presentation Goal: Explain the safety concern clearly and recommend a short-term solution without exaggerating the problem. Draft Slide Sequence: Slide 1 headline and central finding. Slide 2 photo of the crossing area with caption. Slide 3 key evidence from the count and student comments. Slide 4 recommendation for cones and clearer crosswalk markings. Slide 5 source note and next step. Question 1: Which slide should introduce the central finding? {
~A. Slide 1 should include every interview note from the report.#Not correct. Choice A says 'Slide 1 should include every interview note from the report.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
=B. Slide 1 should introduce the central finding so the audience knows the report purpose.#Correct. Step 1: identify the production or presentation skill in the standard. Step 2: connect the choice to the embedded journalism source. This answer works because it supports coherent reporting, accurate visual communication, clear sequence, audience understanding, or credible evidence.
~C. Slide 1 should use only a decorative title with no finding.#Not correct. Choice C says 'Slide 1 should use only a decorative title with no finding.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
~D. Slide 1 should start with the final source note only.#Not correct. Choice D says 'Slide 1 should start with the final source note only.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
}
